{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1524","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1524","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1524\",\"parent_revision\":\"b16d563a01415274d8b14e0222a8ee90f2672afa\",\"root_revision\":\"b784adcab22de557b475df5b4248f531e6e168dc7d20c5d31befaebd4a2df610\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `live_validation` field was added to the language manifest schema and the feature-verifier agent was updated to read it during session 2026-04-05. Neither has been exercised against a real project in any language. The field format, language detection logic, absent-field handling, failure propagation to GAPS_FOUND, and the `agent-browser` sentinel path are all untested. Language plugin authors have no validated examples to follow for any stack (Python, TypeScript, Go, Ruby, C, Rust). It is not known whether the feature-verifier correctly reads the field from `.dh/language-manifest.yaml`, correctly runs the declared command, or correctly surfaces the gap when the field is absent.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: live_validation manifest field: testing, validation and improvement\\nDate: 2026-04-05\\nGoal: Validate that the feature-verifier correctly reads and acts on quality_gates.live_validation across all four branches, and add working examples to Python language manifests.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. live_validation field schema documented in language-manifest-schema.md | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep confirmed lines 75-87 of language-manifest-schema.md\\n2. Feature-verifier 4-branch logic (run / gap / agent-browser / no manifest) implemented | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed Step 8 in feature-verifier.md; zero real-invocation tests\\n3. Python manifests (python3-cli, python3) lack live_validation field | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed python3-cli has NO quality_gates section at all\\n4. No tests exist for feature-verifier live_validation behavior | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep confirmed test_live_validation.py tests backlog server L1-L11 lifecycle only\\n5. Appropriate live_validation command for python3-cli delivery surface | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: python3-cli manifest tests CLI entry point \u2014 command derivable from existing quality_gates.test pattern\\n6. Appropriate live_validation command for python3 base manifest | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: python3 base manifest delivery surface determinable from manifest structure\\n7. Test infrastructure pattern for feature-verifier behavior testing | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst identified test file location and pattern from existing tests\\n8. Gap propagation from absent live_validation to GAPS_FOUND | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: feature-verifier.md lines confirm gap recording and evidence block format\\n\\nNew conditions discovered by swarm:\\n9. python3-cli manifest has NO quality_gates section \u2014 entire block must be added | (new) AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst file read confirmed\\n10. manifest_schema.py / quality_gates.py / manifest_resolver.py / manifest_merge.py exist in data path | (new) AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker wave 2 grep-confirmed all four\\n11. test_live_validation.py naming collision with backlog server tests | (new) AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst + fact-checker wave 2 confirmed file tests L1-L11 backlog lifecycle\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (delivery surface determined from manifest structure)\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (base manifest structure derivable)\\n- Condition 7: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (test infra pattern confirmed by impact-analyst)\\n- Condition 8: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (feature-verifier.md confirms gap recording)\\n- Conditions 9-11: NEW AVAILABLE (discovered by swarm)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\nAVAILABLE count: 11\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3-cli/language-manifest.yaml` \u2014 Will gain `quality_gates.live_validation` field. Currently the file has no `quality_gates` section at all (only `project_detection` and `stage_skills`). Adding live_validation requires first adding the entire `quality_gates` block. Appropriate command must be determined for the `typer-cli` delivery surface (likely `uv run {entrypoint} --version` or `uv run {entrypoint} --help`). | Risk: HIGH | Why: No existing quality_gates section \u2014 entire block must be added; appropriate live command for typer-cli surface is DERIVABLE (item RT-ICA #5), not confirmed.\\n\\n- `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml` \u2014 Will gain `quality_gates.live_validation` field. File already has a `quality_gates` section with format/lint/typecheck/test/standards. Adding `live_validation` is a single-field addition. Appropriate command for the library/package delivery surface must be determined. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Existing quality_gates section lowers risk; command selection for library surface (not CLI) requires judgment about what \\\"live delivery surface\\\" means for a generic Python package.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md::Step 8` \u2014 Primary consumer. Step 8 implements the 4-branch live_validation logic (run command / gap-report / agent-browser / no-manifest). Logic is implemented but has never been exercised against a real manifest. Bugs surfaced during testing will require edits to this agent. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Zero real-invocation exercise means all 4 branches are structurally present but behaviorally unverified; testing will likely surface at least one gap requiring an agent edit.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_schema.py` \u2014 References `quality_gates` in schema. `live_validation` must be added to the schema's quality_gates field model for validation to accept the field without warnings or errors. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Schema validation of manifests goes through this file; if live_validation is not declared in schema, new manifest content may fail validation or be silently dropped.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 Python model for quality gates. May need `live_validation: str | None = None` field added to the QualityGates dataclass/Pydantic model. If absent, the field may not be passed through to the feature-verifier at runtime. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: If the model doesn't declare the field, ruamel.yaml or Pydantic parsing may drop it silently when loading manifests.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_resolver.py` \u2014 Resolves and merges language manifests at runtime. Must pass `live_validation` through to the feature-verifier's execution context. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: If resolver ignores unknown quality_gates subkeys, the field will not reach the feature-verifier's Step 8 regardless of what the manifest declares.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_merge.py` \u2014 Merges manifests (extends chain: python3-cli extends python3). live_validation declared in python3-cli should take precedence over python3's. Merge behavior for this new field must be correct. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: python3-cli extends python3 via `extends: python3-development:python3`; merge order for quality_gates subkeys must be verified for live_validation.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/README.md` \u2014 References `live_validation` (confirmed via grep). May document the field as part of quality gates overview. If content becomes inconsistent with the validated behavior, it becomes misleading. | Risk: LOW | Why: README is informational; content drift is low-severity but should be checked.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` \u2014 **Critical naming collision.** This file currently tests the **backlog MCP server live lifecycle** (L1\u2013L11: backlog_add, backlog_list, backlog_view, backlog_update, backlog_groom, backlog_sync, backlog_pull, backlog_close, backlog_resolve). It does NOT test feature-verifier live_validation behavior. The item states this file is the intended location for new tests. Either: (a) new feature-verifier tests must go in a different file (e.g., `test_feature_verifier_live_validation.py`), or (b) the file name must be changed and both test suites separated. Proceeding without resolving this collision creates a false sense of coverage. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Naming collision risks new tests being placed in the wrong file or a misread of existing coverage; the e2e marks on existing tests (skip when GITHUB_TOKEN absent) must not be inherited by new feature-verifier unit tests.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_manifest_schema.py` \u2014 Tests manifest schema validation. If `live_validation` is added to the schema model, this test file needs new cases: (a) manifest with live_validation present \u2192 validates, (b) manifest without live_validation \u2192 validates with field absent, (c) live_validation set to \\\"agent-browser\\\" \u2192 validates. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: No coverage for live_validation validation rules currently exists; missing tests leave schema behavior unverified.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_manifest_resolver.py` \u2014 Tests manifest resolution. Needs test that live_validation is correctly passed through the resolver to the resolved manifest output. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Resolver passthrough is a key link; no test currently confirms live_validation survives resolution.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_manifest_merge.py` \u2014 Tests manifest merge behavior. Needs test for live_validation field merge precedence when python3-cli extends python3 (child overrides parent). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Merge behavior for new quality_gates subkeys is unverified.\\n\\n- `tests/test_quality_gates.py` \u2014 Tests quality gates. May need live_validation field tested in the QualityGates model. | Risk: LOW | Why: Depends on whether sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py is updated; if the model gains the field, this test file needs coverage.\\n\\n- `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` \u2014 Integration test for quality gates. May need live_validation integration path tested. | Risk: LOW | Why: Integration path only relevant if resolver and model changes are made.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/language-manifest-schema.md` \u2014 ALREADY documents `live_validation` field with examples, rules, and sentinel value `agent-browser`. Content is current. After testing validates actual behavior, verify that examples remain accurate (especially the absent-field gap-report wording). | Risk: LOW | Why: Documentation is ahead of implementation; content is correct but should be spot-checked post-testing.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/templates/language-manifest-template.md` \u2014 ALREADY includes `live_validation` with inline comments and examples. Correct and current. | Risk: LOW | Why: Template is already correct; no change needed unless example commands need updating after Python manifest decisions are made.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/final-verification/SKILL.md` \u2014 References feature-verifier behavior and live delivery surface validation. If Step 8 logic is refined during testing, this skill's guidance on when GAPS_FOUND is triggered may need updating. | Risk: LOW | Why: Skill describes the outcome (VERIFIED / GAPS_FOUND) rather than the implementation detail; refinements to Step 8 are unlikely to change the described outcome.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 References feature-verifier as part of the completion workflow. Live validation failure now blocks VERIFIED status. Skill may need a note that live_validation absent produces SKIPPED (not FAIL). | Risk: LOW | Why: Behavioral nuance \u2014 absent live_validation is a gap (not a hard failure); skill instructions should be consistent with that.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Documents feature-verifier in the workflow diagram. Step 8 is a new verification layer added in the same session; may not yet appear in the architecture diagram. | Risk: LOW | Why: Diagram drift is documentation risk only; does not affect runtime behavior.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 References `live_validation` (confirmed via grep). CI runs pytest test suite. New feature-verifier tests must NOT be marked `e2e` (unlike the existing `test_live_validation.py` tests which skip without GITHUB_TOKEN). If new tests accidentally inherit `e2e` marks, they will silently be excluded from default CI runs. The `validate-plugins` job runs `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/` \u2014 if schema validation is tightened to reject unknown quality_gates fields, the new manifests must pass validation before CI can merge. The `manifest-sync` job (`prek run auto-sync-manifests`) will pick up manifest YAML changes. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Test marking discipline is critical \u2014 e2e skip-without-token must not apply to unit tests; manifest-sync job will run against the new YAML content.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 Listed as both producer (the Step 8 instruction block) and consumer (the agent that reads and acts on the field). Step 8 declares all 4 branches; validation against real manifests may reveal: (a) file-path resolution bugs for `.dh/language-manifest.yaml`, (b) command execution environment issues (working directory, shell), (c) absent-field gap-report wording that doesn't match the schema doc wording. Any of these require agent edits. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Untested instruction code is the core risk of this item; the agent is both the subject of testing and a potential target of fixes.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 References language manifest for workflow setup. If language manifest loading now requires live_validation for a VERIFIED result, language plugin authors following this skill may be prompted to add it. Current skill content likely doesn't mention this requirement. | Risk: LOW | Why: Skill guides feature addition workflow, not manifest authoring; low likelihood of breakage.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/execution/SKILL.md` \u2014 References language manifest in execution stage context. | Risk: LOW | Why: Execution stage does not invoke feature-verifier; live_validation not in scope here.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` \u2014 References language manifest. | Risk: LOW | Why: Task decomposition stage does not invoke feature-verifier; no live_validation interaction.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3-cli/language-manifest.yaml` | Role: producer | Connection: Will gain live_validation field; currently lacks quality_gates entirely | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml` | Role: producer | Connection: Will gain live_validation field under existing quality_gates | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: Step 8 reads and acts on quality_gates.live_validation from .dh/language-manifest.yaml | Action: MULTIPLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_schema.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Schema validation of quality_gates fields; live_validation must be declared | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Python model for quality gates; live_validation field must be declared | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_resolver.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Resolves manifest at runtime; must pass live_validation through | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_merge.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Merges manifests for extends chain; live_validation merge precedence must be correct | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: Name collision \u2014 tests backlog server, not feature-verifier; naming resolution required before new tests are placed | Action: MULTIPLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_manifest_schema.py` | Role: test | Connection: Schema validation tests; live_validation validation rules need coverage | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_manifest_resolver.py` | Role: test | Connection: Resolver tests; live_validation passthrough needs coverage | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_manifest_merge.py` | Role: test | Connection: Merge tests; live_validation field merge precedence needs coverage | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `tests/test_quality_gates.py` | Role: test | Connection: Quality gate model tests; may need live_validation field | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` | Role: test | Connection: Integration tests for quality gates | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/language-manifest-schema.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Documents live_validation field; already current | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/templates/language-manifest-template.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Template already has live_validation; verify examples after command choices made | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/final-verification/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: References feature-verifier outcome model; GAPS_FOUND trigger may need nuance update | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: References feature-verifier; absent live_validation is gap not fail \u2014 may need clarification | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` | Role: ci | Connection: Runs pytest; new tests must not inherit e2e marks; manifest-sync job picks up YAML changes | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/README.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: References live_validation field; verify content after behavior is confirmed | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: **MEDIUM**\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` \u2014 naming collision with unrelated backlog server tests; placing feature-verifier tests here without resolving the collision creates false coverage signals\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 Step 8 is structurally complete but zero real-invocation test coverage; testing will surface bugs requiring agent edits\\n  - `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3-cli/language-manifest.yaml` \u2014 requires quality_gates section addition plus correct live command selection for typer-cli surface (currently DERIVABLE, not confirmed)\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - verification (all 4 branches untested in real invocations)\\n  - scope (test_live_validation.py naming collision expands the scope of test infrastructure decisions)\\n  - compatibility (schema/model files may need live_validation field declared to avoid silent field-drop during manifest loading)\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_schema.py`, `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py`, `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_resolver.py`, and `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_merge.py` were not in the original item description but are in the live_validation data path and must be verified compatible. The `test_live_validation.py` naming collision is a scope discovery that affects where new tests can safely be placed.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (manifest_schema, quality_gates model, resolver, merge chain)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **live_validation manifest field: testing, validation and improvement** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-04-05: live_validation added to language manifest schema and feature-verifier in the same session as this backlog item \u2014 no real-project exercise has occurred\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-05)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 the field was added in the same session that introduced it; every project using the development harness is exposed to unvalidated behavior. A gap or false-pass in live_validation silently weakens the verification step for all users.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- 2 Python manifests gain a new required quality gate field (python3-cli needs entire quality_gates section; python3 needs single field addition)\\n- Feature-verifier gets its first real-invocation test coverage for Step 8 (4 branches)\\n- Language plugin authors get a validated reference for each delivery surface type\\n- test_live_validation.py naming collision resolved by creating distinct test file\\n- Python model files (manifest_schema.py, quality_gates.py) confirmed via fact-check as NOT containing live_validation \u2014 scope expansion decision needed: either add the field to the Python models or confirm feature-verifier reads raw YAML bypassing the schema pipeline\\n- manifest_resolver.py and manifest_merge.py confirmed via fact-check as having 0 live_validation references \u2014 verify compatibility only if Python models are updated\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Developers using dh:final-verification get accurate live delivery validation\\n- Language plugin authors have working examples to copy for their own manifests\\n- The absence-gap message is exercised, ensuring it surfaces correctly in GAPS_FOUND\\n- agent-browser sentinel path is confirmed to record DEFERRED_BROWSER (not a failure)\\n- Python manifest data path clarity: fact-check establishes whether live_validation flows through Python models or is read as raw YAML by the agent\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n1. Feature-verifier reads `.dh/language-manifest.yaml`, finds `quality_gates.live_validation`, runs the declared command verbatim, records pass/fail with full stdout+stderr.\\n2. When field is absent: records `LIVE_VALIDATION: SKIPPED \u2014 no live_validation command declared in language manifest.` and sets GAPS_FOUND.\\n3. When field is `agent-browser`: records `LIVE_VALIDATION: DEFERRED_BROWSER` and does NOT set GAPS_FOUND.\\n4. Python3-cli manifest: `live_validation` command invokes the CLI entry point (e.g., `uv run {entrypoint} --version`).\\n5. Python3 base manifest: `live_validation` command appropriate for library/MCP server delivery surface.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Test: feature-verifier reads live_validation from fixture manifest and runs the declared command \u2014 exit 0 \u2192 no gap recorded\\n- [ ] Test: feature-verifier reads live_validation from fixture manifest and command exits non-zero \u2192 GAPS_FOUND set\\n- [ ] Test: feature-verifier reads live_validation = `agent-browser` \u2192 DEFERRED_BROWSER recorded, no GAPS_FOUND\\n- [ ] Test: feature-verifier reads manifest with absent live_validation \u2192 exact gap message present in report, GAPS_FOUND set\\n- [ ] Test: feature-verifier reads from path `.dh/language-manifest.yaml` (not `.yml` variant) unless fallback is documented\\n- [ ] `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3-cli/language-manifest.yaml` declares `quality_gates.live_validation` with a working CLI invocation command\\n- [ ] `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml` declares `quality_gates.live_validation` with a working library/MCP invocation command\\n- [ ] All new tests pass under `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/ -k live_validation_manifest`\\n- [ ] No regression in existing test_live_validation.py (backlog server tests) \u2014 naming collision resolved by using a distinct test file name\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n- Language manifest schema: `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/language-manifest-schema.md` (lines 75-87)\\n- Feature-verifier Step 8 logic: `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` (lines 270-340)\\n- Language manifest template: `plugins/development-harness/templates/language-manifest-template.md`\\n- Discovery artifact: registered on issue #1524 as feature-context\\n- Fact-check evidence: manifest_schema.py:49-57 (QualityGates fields), quality_gates.py:24-73 (phase definitions), manifest_resolver.py (0 matches), manifest_merge.py:66-134 (extends chain)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNo external blockers. All information is AVAILABLE (RT-ICA: APPROVED, 11 AVAILABLE, 0 MISSING).\\n\\nFact-check caveat: 4 of 6 data-path claims were REFUTED \u2014 the Python manifest pipeline does not contain live_validation. Implementation must determine the actual data flow before modifying these files.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nNARROW-STANDARD. Two manifest edits (straightforward) + one new test file (4 test cases, fixture manifests needed). Estimated: 1 focused session.\\n\\nRisk factor: if implementation determines live_validation flows through the Python schema pipeline (not raw YAML), scope expands to 4 additional files + their test files. This would upgrade effort to STANDARD.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**To modify:**\\n- `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3-cli/language-manifest.yaml` \u2014 add entire quality_gates section including live_validation (fact-check confirmed: NO quality_gates section exists)\\n- `plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml` \u2014 add live_validation field under existing quality_gates section\\n\\n**To create:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_feature_verifier_live_validation.py` \u2014 new test file (distinct from existing backlog server test to resolve naming collision)\\n\\n**To verify (read-only):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 confirm Step 8 logic matches test expectations\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/language-manifest-schema.md` \u2014 confirm gap message format\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` \u2014 confirm no tests are inadvertently affected\\n\\n**Scope expansion candidates (fact-check: live_validation NOT present in any):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_schema.py` \u2014 QualityGates dataclass has format/lint/typecheck/test/standards only; live_validation field absent (REFUTED by fact-check)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 defines phase definitions, NOT quality_gates model fields; live_validation absent (REFUTED by fact-check)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_resolver.py` \u2014 0 matches for live_validation (REFUTED by fact-check)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_merge.py` \u2014 extends handling exists but 0 live_validation references (PARTIALLY VERIFIED by fact-check)\\n\\nDecision needed during implementation: determine whether feature-verifier reads raw YAML (bypassing Python models) or flows through the schema pipeline. If the latter, all 4 scope-expansion files need live_validation added.\\n\\n## Wave 2 Expanded Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Claim 1: manifest_schema.py exists and contains quality_gates model with live_validation field\\n**Verdict:** REFUTED\\n**Evidence:** plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_schema.py:49-57 \u2014 `QualityGates` dataclass defines fields: `format`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `standards`. **NO `live_validation` field.**\\n**Source:** plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_schema.py, line 49-57\\n\\n### Claim 2: sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py models quality_gates with live_validation field\\n**Verdict:** REFUTED\\n**Evidence:** plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py:1-73 defines `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` with 6 task phases (Code Review, Feature Verification, Integration Check, Documentation Dri